      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "The equation ${log}_{5}⁡5=1$ is equivalent to ${b}^{1}=5.$ What is the value of $b?$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n${log}_{b}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={b}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare ${log}_{5}⁡5=1$ with ${log}_{b}⁡a=x,$ we get $a=5,$ $b=5,$ and $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to ${5}^{1}=5.$ Consequently, $b=5.$",
